## std.video.vp9 (spec std.vpx.1-6, ADR 0989): a VP9 video decoder in AIL.
## Profile 0 (8-bit, 4:2:0). Frames come out as I420 planes; `Frame.rgba`
## converts one for drawing. Decoding follows the VP9 bitstream specification
## and libvpx (BSD-3-Clause, see NOTICE), whose output it matches bit for bit.
## Not yet supported: profiles 1-3, and references of a different size
## (scaled prediction); both fail with a Vp9Error.

## Why a frame could not be decoded (std.vpx.1).
pub error struct Vp9Error "vp9: {self.why}"
    pub why str

## One decoded picture (std.vpx.3): I420 planes without padding. `y` has
## `width * height` bytes; `u` and `v` have `cw() * ch()` bytes each, the
## chroma size rounded up. `space` is the stream's colour space (1 BT.601,
## 2 BT.709, 0 unknown; VP9 spec 7.2.2) and `full_range` its range.
pub struct Frame
    pub width int
    pub height int
    pub y bytes
    pub u bytes
    pub v bytes
    pub space int
    pub full_range bool

## The chroma plane width and height (std.vpx.3).
pub fn Frame.cw(self) int
    (self.width + 1) / 2

pub fn Frame.ch(self) int
    (self.height + 1) / 2

# Block sizes (libvpx BLOCK_SIZE order).
B4X4 := 0
B4X8 := 1
B8X4 := 2
B8X8 := 3
B64X64 := 12
N8W := [1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 2, 2, 2, 4, 4, 4, 8, 8]
N8H := [1, 1, 1, 1, 2, 1, 2, 4, 2, 4, 8, 4, 8]
